  "articleBody": "Upgrading bathroom trim or fixing door frames looks straightforward until you encounter hidden moisture, out-of-plumb walls, or tricky tile transitions. Knowing when to step back and call a professional carpenter saves you time and protects your home from hidden water damage.\n\nSigns It Is Time to Call a Professional\n- The door sticks or scrapes the floor despite hinge adjustments, pointing to a racked or out-of-plumb rough opening.\n- Wood at the base of the door jamb or baseboard feels soft, spongy, or discolored from trapped water.\n- Trim needs to terminate against newly installed shower tile, requiring precise scribing and continuous water-resistant sealant.\n- Your walls or floors are noticeably out of level, meaning standard miter cuts will leave ugly gaps that caulk cannot hide.\n- Water damage has penetrated the drywall into the structural wall studs or subflooring behind the casing.\n- You want seamless finish carpentry, such as custom wainscoting or crown molding, with crisp joints that withstand heavy bathroom humidity.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nBathroom environments leave zero margin for error. A seasoned carpenter not only fits tight joints but also understands how to properly seal end grain, shim frames plumb, and coordinate repairs without disturbing adjacent drywall or tile.\n\nIf your bathroom door frame or trim needs skilled hands, call Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to schedule an on-site evaluation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}